.TH WMCOREMAP 1 "October 2026" "wmcoremap 0.1" "Window Maker dockapps"
.SH NAME
wmcoremap \- per-core CPU load heatmap dockapp for Window Maker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmcoremap
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmcoremap
is a 64x64 dockapp that shows every logical CPU as one LED in a grid. The
colour of each LED follows that CPU's load, in the colours of wmsysmon:
dark grey-green when idle, bright green under moderate load, then yellow,
orange and red near 100%. LEDs shrink when there are too many CPUs for
the chosen size, so it works for a handful of cores as well as for
machines with a hundred or more. A CPU that is offline is drawn as a hollow
ring.
.PP
The bottom row shows total CPU use and the CPU temperature. Left click
cycles through these screens, whose name appears in the top left corner:
.TP
.B CPU
the per-core heatmap; the number at the top right is the CPU count.
.TP
.B LOAD
total CPU use over the last 54 samples.
.TP
.B TEMP
CPU temperature over the last 54 samples (only when a sensor is found).
.TP
.B GPU
GPU busy percentage over time, with VRAM use in the bottom row (only for
AMD cards on the amdgpu driver).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " display"
X display to connect to.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-celsius
Show temperatures in degrees Celsius (the default).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-fahrenheit
Show temperatures in degrees Fahrenheit.
.TP
.BI \-interval " ms"
Update period in milliseconds (default 1000). The history screens cover
54 updates.
.TP
.BI \-screen " cpu|load|temp|gpu"
Screen to show at start (default \fBcpu\fR).
.TP
.BI \-sensor " path"
Temperature input to read, in millidegrees Celsius, e.g.
\fI/sys/class/hwmon/hwmon1/temp1_input\fR. By default the k10temp,
zenpower, coretemp, cpu_thermal and soc_thermal hwmon drivers are tried,
then the x86_pkg_temp and acpitz thermal zones.
.TP
.BI \-fg " color"
Text colour (default #20B2AE).
.TP
.BI \-bg " color"
Background colour (default #202020).
.TP
.BR \-size " " small | medium | large
LED size; one of the words
.BR small ,
.B medium
or
.B large
(the default):
.RS
.TP 8
.B small
4x4 pixel LEDs spaced 1 pixel apart, as in wmsysmon
.TP
.B medium
6x6 pixel LEDs
.TP
.B large
9x9 pixel LEDs
.RE
.IP
With too many CPUs for the chosen size the LEDs are made smaller.
.TP
.B \-square
Draw square cells instead of round LEDs.
.TP
.BI \-fake " n"
Simulate \fIn\fR CPUs with synthetic load, to see how the grid looks on a
larger machine.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-help
Show a summary of the options.
.SH MOUSE
.TP
.B Left
Next screen.
.TP
.B Wheel
Previous / next screen.
.TP
.B Right
Switch between Celsius and Fahrenheit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/stat
Per-CPU time counters.
.TP
.I /sys/class/hwmon/*/temp*_input, /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/temp
Temperature sensors.
.TP
.I /sys/class/drm/card*/device/gpu_busy_percent
AMD GPU load (amdgpu driver only).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmaker (1),
.BR wmtop (1),
.BR wmsysmon (1)
